{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Performance","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"ScreenStates’ pitch is “small, dependency-free, drop into any screen.” This article covers the three ways that’s kept measurable rather than just assumed: a CI-enforced size budget, an audited concurrency guarantee, and a documented rendering characteristic.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"The-binary-size-budget","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The binary-size budget"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"CI builds "},{"code":"swift build -c release","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on every push and sums the resulting "},{"code":".o","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sizes for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScreenStates","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" target, failing the build if that total exceeds the budget committed in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".github\/binary-size-budget.json"},{"text":". There’s no single linked artifact to measure instead — the library product is “automatic,” and nothing in the package’s own build graph links it standalone — so the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".o"},{"text":" total is the closest deterministic proxy available.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A legitimate feature addition that grows this total past the budget isn’t blocked forever: bump "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxBytes"},{"type":"text","text":" in that file as part of the same PR, the same way a dependency lockfile gets updated alongside the change that needed it. The job never bumps it on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The Task lifecycle guarantee","anchor":"The-Task-lifecycle-guarantee"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refresh","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refreshCollection","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadWithRetry"},{"type":"text","text":" each store their running "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" in a private "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"currentTask"},{"type":"text","text":" property, read by "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/cancel()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"type":"text","text":". Every one of those "},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s captures "},{"code":"self","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as "},{"code":"[weak self]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", not strongly — audited specifically to rule out a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"self -> currentTask -> closure -> self"},{"type":"text","text":" retain cycle keeping a store alive after its last external reference is dropped."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In practice, a completed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" releases its closure’s captures on return regardless of capture style, so this mostly matters for a still-"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"running"}]},{"text":" operation: without ","type":"text"},{"code":"[weak self]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a store couldn’t become eligible for deallocation until that operation finished, even once every other reference to it was already gone. See ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation"},{"type":"text","text":" for the rest of the "},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lifecycle — cancellation, overlapping calls, and the automatic cancel-on-"},{"code":"deinit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" safety net this guarantee supports.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Re-render-characteristics-of-the-default-placeholders","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Re-render characteristics of the default placeholders"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/isRefreshing"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshError"},{"text":" only ever go active once ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refresh(_:)"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshCollection(_:)"},{"text":" have confirmed ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"text":" is already ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"text":" — both fall back to ","type":"text"},{"code":"load(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"loadCollection(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" otherwise, which never touch either property. That means ","type":"text"},{"code":"isRefreshing","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"refreshError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" can never be observed alongside ","type":"text"},{"code":".empty","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"code":".error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so none of the three default placeholders can ever be on screen mid-refresh.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A parent view that reads ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.state","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (via ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") and ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.isRefreshing","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"refreshError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the same ","type":"text"},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the pattern ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" uses for a refresh toast — still has its ","type":"text"},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" re-evaluated whenever either changes, same as any ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property read in a SwiftUI ","type":"text"},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". This guarantee is about ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"which","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" placeholder that re-evaluation could ever affect, not about avoiding the re-evaluation itself: since a default placeholder is only ever on screen while ","type":"text"},{"code":"isRefreshing","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"refreshError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are both inactive, that re-evaluation never has a placeholder to needlessly re-render in the first place — only whatever renders the ","type":"text"},{"code":".data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" case could be affected.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"Performance","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"hierarc